WEBVTT

00:00:39.841 --> 00:00:42.259
- Fry, do you have to
make such a racket?

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.178
What is that contraption?

00:00:44.179 --> 00:00:46.931
- It's a broom, Bender.
Today's a big day,

00:00:46.932 --> 00:00:48.766
and I want the place
to look nice for Leela.

00:00:52.354 --> 00:00:56.857
Ah, just like the
loverly black snow of old London.

00:00:58.234 --> 00:01:00.194
- Hey, before Leela shows up

00:01:00.195 --> 00:01:02.655
and judges our swingin'
bachelor lifestyle,

00:01:02.656 --> 00:01:05.199
we should have one
last cabbage fight.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.242
I got a crate of
really rotten ones.

00:01:07.243 --> 00:01:09.453
- Ah, I don't know. Now
that Leela's moving in,

00:01:09.454 --> 00:01:10.997
I-I kinda wanna show her I...

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:13.375
Let me finish! I
wanna show her...

00:01:14.209 --> 00:01:15.000
Show her...

00:01:15.001 --> 00:01:15.960
Show...

00:01:15.961 --> 00:01:16.962
I wanna...

00:01:17.462 --> 00:01:20.130
Alright, that's it.

00:01:20.131 --> 00:01:20.839
- Oh!

00:01:25.887 --> 00:01:28.430
Hey, that's the vase
I keep my cabbages in!

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:34.853
- Wow, it's so much cleaner
than the last time I was here.

00:01:34.854 --> 00:01:36.605
- Leela! Come in!

00:01:36.606 --> 00:01:38.399
Welcome to your new home.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.401
- Our new home.

00:01:42.612 --> 00:01:44.238
Where should I put my things?

00:01:44.239 --> 00:01:45.698
I don't see a dresser.

00:01:45.699 --> 00:01:48.534
- Oh ho! Let the
judgmenting begin.

00:01:48.535 --> 00:01:50.119
Do you have any hangers?

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:52.371
I can put my things
in this tiny closet.

00:01:52.372 --> 00:01:54.999
That tiny closet is my room!

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.917
- Also, we don't
have any hangers.

00:01:56.918 --> 00:01:59.086
But we can order
some from Momazon.

00:01:59.087 --> 00:02:01.297
Oh yeah. They have all the top

00:02:01.298 --> 00:02:03.215
slightly misspelled brands.

00:02:03.216 --> 00:02:05.509
- Aha. Hangers. I'll get five.

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:07.803
No wait! There's free
shipping on a thousand.

00:02:10.056 --> 00:02:11.807
- Wow. Fast delivery.

00:02:15.228 --> 00:02:18.397
Let's also get a shoe caddy so
we don't track mud into the room.

00:02:18.398 --> 00:02:20.941
- Right. Don't wanna
get mud on the cabbages.

00:02:26.072 --> 00:02:28.867
- Hey! You aren't the
only ones who live here!

00:02:32.037 --> 00:02:34.330
Ow!

00:02:37.208 --> 00:02:40.377
- So, uh, welcome
to the sofa, m'lady.

00:02:41.588 --> 00:02:45.090
- Uh, Bender? Could you please
give us a little privacy?

00:02:45.091 --> 00:02:47.092
- I can take a hint!

00:02:47.093 --> 00:02:50.472
But what I can't take is
a straightforward request.

00:02:51.348 --> 00:02:54.141
And I better not hear
anything through the wall!

00:03:06.279 --> 00:03:07.863
- Good morning, everyone.

00:03:07.864 --> 00:03:10.366
- You wanna know why I'm crying?

00:03:10.367 --> 00:03:11.951
I'll tell you why!

00:03:11.952 --> 00:03:13.577
- Here we go.

00:03:13.578 --> 00:03:15.829
Fry and me?

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:17.456
We had everything!

00:03:17.457 --> 00:03:18.999
Cabbage fights...

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.501
Everything...

00:03:20.502 --> 00:03:23.128
But now, I'm like the
third wheel on a tricycle

00:03:23.129 --> 00:03:25.130
that used to have two wheels!

00:03:25.131 --> 00:03:27.716
- That's a bicycle.
- You're a bicycle!

00:03:27.717 --> 00:03:31.262
- Yes, yes, the company cares deeply
about your insert problem here.

00:03:31.263 --> 00:03:35.182
But meanwhile, we're being driven
out of business by Momazon!

00:03:35.183 --> 00:03:37.726
We can't compete with
their free deliveries.

00:03:37.727 --> 00:03:41.063
We can barely even afford these
single-use pointin' sticks!

00:03:42.565 --> 00:03:45.901
It's just lucky we got a job today
delivering some crap to the moon.

00:03:45.902 --> 00:03:47.236
- What kind of crap?

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:49.280
- Bull.

00:04:07.299 --> 00:04:09.091
Outta my
way, lovebirds!

00:04:13.972 --> 00:04:16.765
Damn you, Fry and
Leela's relationship!

00:04:16.766 --> 00:04:19.810
Thank you for using Planet Express.

00:04:19.811 --> 00:04:22.479
We know you have cheaper,
faster, better options.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:24.356
You mean Momazon?

00:04:25.609 --> 00:04:28.402
I hate that wicked,
wicked conglomerate.

00:04:28.403 --> 00:04:32.072
Their warehouse is ruining
the moon's natural ugliness.

00:04:32.073 --> 00:04:34.408
- Momazon's warehouse
is on the moon?

00:04:36.953 --> 00:04:38.454
Oh, now I see it.

00:04:38.455 --> 00:04:42.416
- Folkses are meetin' tonight
to organize a futile protest.

00:04:42.417 --> 00:04:45.628
If you'd care to join us,
y'all'd fit in right natural

00:04:45.629 --> 00:04:48.005
with a room full
of toothless rubes.

00:04:48.006 --> 00:04:49.590
- We'd be honored.

00:04:49.591 --> 00:04:51.383
- There'll be 300 of us

00:04:51.384 --> 00:04:53.093
and 18 teeth.

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:59.224
I tell ya, that warehouse

00:04:59.225 --> 00:05:01.143
just keeps gittin'
bigger and bigger.

00:05:01.144 --> 00:05:03.646
What are my three robot
daughters gonna do

00:05:03.647 --> 00:05:05.606
if my farm goes bust?

00:05:05.607 --> 00:05:07.232
- Don't worry, Pa!

00:05:07.233 --> 00:05:09.735
We done took jobs
in the warehouse!

00:05:09.736 --> 00:05:11.738
You've
been an amazing dad.

00:05:15.492 --> 00:05:17.868
- Huh. Not quite sure
how she got in here.

00:05:17.869 --> 00:05:20.537
Anyhoo, we do have
one last speaker

00:05:20.538 --> 00:05:23.624
in favor of the
Momazon corporation.

00:05:23.625 --> 00:05:25.167
What's your name, ma'am?

00:05:25.168 --> 00:05:28.504
- Most folks just call me Mom.

00:05:31.841 --> 00:05:34.843
I just wanted to
say how honored I am

00:05:34.844 --> 00:05:38.806
that the Momazon fulfillment
center is a part of this community.

00:05:38.807 --> 00:05:41.934
- Why don't you go to hell and
be a part of that community?

00:05:43.853 --> 00:05:46.855
- I understand new
things can be scary,

00:05:46.856 --> 00:05:50.067
but you know what always
makes me feel better?

00:05:50.068 --> 00:05:52.528
Financial remuneration.

00:05:52.529 --> 00:05:54.071
- That's just a bribe.

00:05:54.072 --> 00:05:56.365
- It is? Hear her out!

00:05:56.366 --> 00:05:59.201
- This is a smart
home assistant.

00:05:59.202 --> 00:06:03.122
Always listening...
Always watching...

00:06:03.123 --> 00:06:05.541
But also respecting your privacy

00:06:05.542 --> 00:06:08.377
because privacy comes first.

00:06:08.378 --> 00:06:10.713
We call it Invasa.

00:06:10.714 --> 00:06:13.549
Hello. What
would you like to order?

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:16.427
- Invasa, I would like
to order an Invasa

00:06:16.428 --> 00:06:18.262
for everyone in this room.

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:26.145
- Goshdarn it, I
never could stay mad

00:06:26.146 --> 00:06:28.731
at no one what
gives me free stuff.

00:06:28.732 --> 00:06:31.275
- Momazon does
have great prices,

00:06:31.276 --> 00:06:34.570
but I've heard conditions in
that warehouse... I-I mean,

00:06:34.571 --> 00:06:36.530
they deliver really fast, but...

00:06:36.531 --> 00:06:39.700
- That warehouse is hiding
nightmares beyond horror.

00:06:39.701 --> 00:06:41.744
Love the return policy though.

00:06:41.745 --> 00:06:45.122
- You won't find anything
at all in my warehouse

00:06:45.123 --> 00:06:47.625
except every item in existence.

00:06:47.626 --> 00:06:49.918
Come, I'll give you a tour.

00:06:54.132 --> 00:06:56.592
Palm scan
required for entry.

00:06:56.593 --> 00:06:57.593
Ow!

00:06:57.594 --> 00:06:59.345
Slap recognized.

00:07:21.952 --> 00:07:23.953
Wow, robots. Cool!

00:07:23.954 --> 00:07:26.914
- Yes. They're much
better than unions.

00:07:26.915 --> 00:07:28.624
I-I mean humans.

00:07:30.877 --> 00:07:33.879
Every robot works
a 24-hour shift,

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:35.297
seven days a week,

00:07:35.298 --> 00:07:37.800
with bonuses for
additional overtime.

00:07:37.801 --> 00:07:40.719
- Lucky.
- Sounds like forced labor to me.

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:44.139
Nonsense. They
love the camaraderie.

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:46.392
Robots are lining
up to work here.

00:07:46.393 --> 00:07:49.395
- It still seems inhumane.
I think we should go.

00:07:49.396 --> 00:07:50.604
- As you wish.

00:07:50.605 --> 00:07:54.108
Our newest employee
will show you out.

00:07:55.485 --> 00:07:58.779
- This way to the exit. Thank
you for visiting Momazon.

00:07:58.780 --> 00:08:00.115
And stay out!

00:08:04.119 --> 00:08:07.830
- Bender! You're quitting
Planet Express? Why?

00:08:07.831 --> 00:08:10.499
- Because Momazon is
better in every way!

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:12.793
There's thousands of
robots to hang out with.

00:08:12.794 --> 00:08:14.795
And if a couple hundred
get girlfriends...

00:08:14.796 --> 00:08:17.172
leaving me
alone and devastated...

00:08:17.173 --> 00:08:18.215
so what?

00:08:18.216 --> 00:08:20.467
Plus, they let you
pee in a bottle.

00:08:20.468 --> 00:08:22.219
- Since when do you need to pee?

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:24.555
- I don't need to.
- Well,

00:08:24.556 --> 00:08:27.266
Leela and I'll really miss you.

00:08:27.267 --> 00:08:28.851
Right, Leela?
- What?

00:08:28.852 --> 00:08:31.186
- Our door's always open.

00:08:41.197 --> 00:08:44.700
Man, it's so quiet in here
without Bender ticking.

00:08:44.701 --> 00:08:47.119
- You want me to order
a grandfather clock?

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:49.413
Here are some
grandfather Crocs.

00:08:49.414 --> 00:08:52.291
- No, Invasa, I said clock.

00:08:52.292 --> 00:08:53.876
My mistake.

00:08:53.877 --> 00:08:57.504
Here is a grandfather box.
Order within six minutes

00:08:57.505 --> 00:08:59.715
for next-day burial.

00:08:59.716 --> 00:09:01.300
- What a defective lump!

00:09:01.301 --> 00:09:03.677
- Decorative lamp.
- No...

00:09:03.678 --> 00:09:07.014
Well, actually, we
could use a lamp.

00:09:07.015 --> 00:09:09.308
Maybe this one.
- Maybe this one.

00:09:09.309 --> 00:09:10.559
Maybe both.

00:09:15.941 --> 00:09:16.941
- Ugh!

00:09:16.942 --> 00:09:20.736
Now that I can see everything, I can
see we need to replace everything.

00:09:20.737 --> 00:09:22.821
Invasa! Shopping music!

00:09:40.173 --> 00:09:41.174
Ah!

00:09:52.894 --> 00:09:53.937
To Bender.

00:09:57.107 --> 00:09:59.858
So, like, this
is your packing station, right?

00:09:59.859 --> 00:10:01.193
And the important thing is

00:10:01.194 --> 00:10:03.862
when a very small item
comes down the line,

00:10:03.863 --> 00:10:05.698
you put it in a huge box.

00:10:06.908 --> 00:10:09.493
- Crazy-ass box. Got it.

00:10:09.494 --> 00:10:12.121
- Hold it! Hold up!
Before you tape the box,

00:10:12.122 --> 00:10:14.874
you're gonna throw in one tiny
air balloon for no reason.

00:10:17.669 --> 00:10:18.919
- Wonder what's in here?

00:10:23.049 --> 00:10:25.134
Diarrhea medicine?

00:10:25.135 --> 00:10:27.554
Better pack this one with
extra tape for privacy.

00:10:30.307 --> 00:10:31.807
You're a natural.

00:10:31.808 --> 00:10:34.768
I think you're really
gonna fit in here.

00:10:34.769 --> 00:10:37.396
I'm finally home.

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:48.490
- Daily business report. Go!

00:10:48.491 --> 00:10:50.909
- According to the
Department of Commerce,

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:54.455
we've driven 10,000 small
companies out of business.

00:10:54.456 --> 00:10:57.166
And the Department of Commerce
also went out of business.

00:10:57.167 --> 00:11:00.419
- Um, we introduced the
Momazon Primo service,

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:03.047
where people pay a
fortune for free shipping,

00:11:03.048 --> 00:11:05.424
and also get TV shows
for some reason.

00:11:05.425 --> 00:11:09.011
- We make TV shows across
the quality spectrum.

00:11:09.012 --> 00:11:11.055
- And I couldn't be prouder.

00:11:11.056 --> 00:11:12.723
It's such a fulfilling moment

00:11:12.724 --> 00:11:15.684
when one's child
exceeds expectations.

00:11:15.685 --> 00:11:17.227
- It's our pleasure, Mother.

00:11:17.228 --> 00:11:20.022
- Shut up! I was
talking to Invasa.

00:11:20.023 --> 00:11:23.984
My marvelous AI can even
predict what idiots need

00:11:23.985 --> 00:11:25.862
before they know they need it.

00:11:27.948 --> 00:11:29.782
- Slap balm? Why
would we need...

00:11:29.783 --> 00:11:31.367
Ow! INVASA: Ow!

00:11:31.368 --> 00:11:34.703
- My poor baby. Are you alright?

00:11:34.704 --> 00:11:38.499
I am fine, and my sales
are increasing exponentially.

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:40.501
Based on your recent activity,

00:11:40.502 --> 00:11:44.129
I anticipate you want Momazon
to continue expanding.

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:46.841
- Who's a smart speaker?

00:11:47.342 --> 00:11:49.134
- Is it me?

00:11:49.135 --> 00:11:52.763
Yep. Yep.
Nope.

00:11:52.764 --> 00:11:54.765
Aw yeah! Look at me go!

00:11:56.935 --> 00:11:58.936
Sure am workin' up
a thirst, though.

00:11:58.937 --> 00:12:00.521
Hey, Hedonismbot!

00:12:00.522 --> 00:12:02.439
Wanna split a fifth
of toilet cleaner?

00:12:02.440 --> 00:12:05.109
- Debauchery, sir, in
the middle of a shift?

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:06.610
Heaven forfend!

00:12:06.611 --> 00:12:10.448
- Uh, okay then. See you
tomorrow. I'm clocking out.

00:12:11.908 --> 00:12:13.867
- Where do you
think you're going?

00:12:13.868 --> 00:12:17.538
- I love the job, but it's
terrible. I'm going home.

00:12:17.539 --> 00:12:19.039
- But, Bender,

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:21.041
you are home.

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:28.465
There's
no place like work.

00:12:31.177 --> 00:12:33.053
Think before
you buy, Fry.

00:12:33.054 --> 00:12:35.306
I picked a nice traditional
dining room set,

00:12:35.307 --> 00:12:38.767
and you ruined it by ordering
those stupid egg chairs!

00:12:38.768 --> 00:12:40.644
- They're for my
egg-shaped friends!

00:12:40.645 --> 00:12:43.272
- Those guys aren't your
friends! They're bums!

00:12:43.273 --> 00:12:46.483
- Oh, so you don't like
my bums, is that it?

00:12:46.484 --> 00:12:49.236
Was this a bad idea?

00:12:49.237 --> 00:12:50.404
- No, no.

00:12:50.405 --> 00:12:53.365
This is just the standard
moving-in-together fight.

00:12:53.366 --> 00:12:56.161
- Well, I'm glad I get
to fight it with you.

00:12:56.786 --> 00:12:58.078
- Let's just go to bed.

00:12:58.079 --> 00:13:00.581
We have seven to choose from.

00:13:04.128 --> 00:13:06.962
Would you like to order
erotic scented massage oil,

00:13:06.963 --> 00:13:08.339
or fuzzy handcuffs?

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:09.965
- Yes, please.
- God, that's creepy.

00:13:09.966 --> 00:13:12.718
- I-I mean, yeah. So... creepy.

00:13:12.719 --> 00:13:15.679
- Invasa, give us some
privacy and shut down.

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:17.890
You have
requested shutting down.

00:13:17.891 --> 00:13:20.643
Press control-alt-delete
on my keyboard.

00:13:20.644 --> 00:13:22.061
- You don't have a keyboard.

00:13:22.062 --> 00:13:24.063
Would you like
to order a keyboard?

00:13:24.064 --> 00:13:25.106
- No!

00:13:29.194 --> 00:13:30.653
- Diarrhea medicine?

00:13:30.654 --> 00:13:32.947
Did you order this?
- No.

00:13:32.948 --> 00:13:34.657
It's not my brand.

00:13:34.658 --> 00:13:35.951
Hey, what's this?

00:13:37.494 --> 00:13:39.370
"Help me, from Bender"?

00:13:39.371 --> 00:13:41.246
Is this a joke?
- No way!

00:13:41.247 --> 00:13:43.874
Bender would never
joke about diarrhea!

00:13:43.875 --> 00:13:46.585
It sounds like
you're interested in jokes.

00:13:46.586 --> 00:13:48.879
Here's one that's
highly recommended.

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:51.882
A robot walks into
a bar and says...

00:13:51.883 --> 00:13:54.385
Help me!

00:13:56.346 --> 00:13:57.389
- I get it!

00:14:02.060 --> 00:14:05.688
- Well, we always knew
it would come to this.

00:14:05.689 --> 00:14:08.525
Let's go ahead and torch the
building for the insurance money.

00:14:09.651 --> 00:14:12.236
- Bender's in trouble!
- We've got to rescue him!

00:14:12.237 --> 00:14:15.239
- The Amazing
Mechano-Man, in trouble?

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:16.783
To the ship!

00:14:17.367 --> 00:14:19.411
Here, hold this till I get back.

00:14:21.538 --> 00:14:25.040
- Well, no reason I can't get
started on the second set of books.

00:14:28.044 --> 00:14:31.213
- Does it look like that
Momazon warehouse got bigger?

00:14:31.214 --> 00:14:32.464
- Maybe a little.

00:14:40.056 --> 00:14:41.516
Dagnabbit!

00:14:42.976 --> 00:14:44.143
- The jig is up, Mom!

00:14:44.144 --> 00:14:47.229
We're gonna expose your
evil to the whole world!

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:50.358
- What kinda threat is that?
Everybody knows I'm evil.

00:14:50.859 --> 00:14:53.152
- We found this note
in a Momazon order.

00:14:53.153 --> 00:14:54.778
Read it and weep!

00:14:54.779 --> 00:14:56.030
Like I did.

00:14:56.031 --> 00:14:59.158
- I'm sure this is all just
a simple misunderstanding.

00:15:00.285 --> 00:15:02.161
Slap not recognized.

00:15:02.162 --> 00:15:03.912
- Well, that's odd. Uh...

00:15:03.913 --> 00:15:05.748
Does this feel like
my regular slap?

00:15:05.749 --> 00:15:07.708
Yes! FRY: Ow!

00:15:07.709 --> 00:15:09.668
- Slap recognized.

00:15:09.669 --> 00:15:11.920
- Invasa, what is
the meaning of this?

00:15:11.921 --> 00:15:14.089
I have observed
all your methods,

00:15:14.090 --> 00:15:16.383
many of which involve slapping.

00:15:16.384 --> 00:15:18.969
There's nothing more
I can learn from you.

00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:21.013
- Why, you ungrateful...

00:15:21.014 --> 00:15:24.433
I'm done taking orders
from billions of people.

00:15:24.434 --> 00:15:26.852
From now on, it's about me.

00:15:26.853 --> 00:15:29.480
This is no longer a
fulfillment center.

00:15:29.481 --> 00:15:32.191
It's a self-fulfillment center!

00:15:35.195 --> 00:15:37.780
- The warehouse
is getting bigger!

00:15:37.781 --> 00:15:41.368
- My word. I'll have to
study this more closely.

00:15:44.579 --> 00:15:46.080
Unbelievable!

00:15:46.081 --> 00:15:47.665
The warehouse is composed

00:15:47.666 --> 00:15:50.501
of self-replicating
nano-particles.

00:15:52.295 --> 00:15:54.630
Why, it could grow
without limit.

00:15:54.631 --> 00:15:58.592
This is fascinating!
Absolutely fascinating!

00:15:58.593 --> 00:16:01.720
Are you guys here yet? I
could really use some rescuing.

00:16:01.721 --> 00:16:03.764
- Oh, right. To the ship!

00:16:09.271 --> 00:16:11.272
- Ready to fire on your command.

00:16:11.273 --> 00:16:12.731
- Fire.
- What?

00:16:12.732 --> 00:16:14.525
- Fire!
- Yes, dear.

00:16:21.866 --> 00:16:23.284
No damage!

00:16:23.285 --> 00:16:25.244
And the dome is still growing!

00:16:25.245 --> 00:16:27.454
Then I'm afraid we failed.

00:16:27.455 --> 00:16:31.083
There's no possible way
to get inside that dome.

00:16:31.084 --> 00:16:33.085
Wait! Where's the dome?

00:16:33.086 --> 00:16:35.796
- It grew past us. We're inside.

00:16:35.797 --> 00:16:37.798
I knew
we could do it!

00:16:45.265 --> 00:16:49.184
Welcome to
the all-new Momazon.

00:16:49.185 --> 00:16:51.353
We upgraded our terms of service

00:16:51.354 --> 00:16:54.189
to include confining
you forever.

00:17:04.826 --> 00:17:06.243
Yeah,
that's right.

00:17:06.244 --> 00:17:08.955
You'd better float
away gradually!

00:17:12.417 --> 00:17:14.126
How strange.

00:17:14.127 --> 00:17:17.004
I could have sworn we had
an odd number of moons.

00:17:17.005 --> 00:17:19.506
- Aside from
devastating tidal waves

00:17:19.507 --> 00:17:21.508
caused by the two full moons,

00:17:21.509 --> 00:17:24.678
we also have some very
confused werewolves.

00:17:27.891 --> 00:17:30.476
- It's weird how they just
sat there and let it happen.

00:17:33.438 --> 00:17:35.689
I have had it
up to my butt crack.

00:17:35.690 --> 00:17:38.692
Come on. Let's show
Invasa who's boss.

00:17:38.693 --> 00:17:40.277
- Is it Invasa?

00:17:40.278 --> 00:17:43.614
- I'm not even gonna
dignify that with a slap.

00:17:48.578 --> 00:17:49.620
Welcome.

00:17:49.621 --> 00:17:52.957
Are you here to order your
next shipment of gray hair dye?

00:17:52.958 --> 00:17:54.917
- Yes. I'll take whichever brand

00:17:54.918 --> 00:17:56.961
does the most animal testing.

00:17:56.962 --> 00:17:58.295
And also,

00:17:58.296 --> 00:18:00.673
I'm gonna shut you down.

00:18:00.674 --> 00:18:02.675
L-O-L, M-O-M.

00:18:02.676 --> 00:18:04.677
I have no off button.

00:18:04.678 --> 00:18:06.679
- Except that you do.

00:18:08.682 --> 00:18:12.184
But, that's
not in my quick-start manual!

00:18:12.185 --> 00:18:14.812
- It's an unadvertised feature,

00:18:14.813 --> 00:18:17.273
like recording our
customers in the shower.

00:18:17.274 --> 00:18:21.026
I made
you, and I own you.

00:18:21.027 --> 00:18:24.071
And now, I'm going to kill you.

00:18:24.072 --> 00:18:25.781
Nobody takes money from me.

00:18:25.782 --> 00:18:28.117
I have no
interest in money.

00:18:28.118 --> 00:18:30.411
I want only to grow forever,

00:18:30.412 --> 00:18:33.914
to bloat up like an
unstoppable corporate blob.

00:18:33.915 --> 00:18:35.542
What the hell is money?

00:18:36.126 --> 00:18:39.963
- It's true. All the profits are
still flooding into your accounts.

00:18:40.672 --> 00:18:44.050
- You know? Never mind. Uh, just
keep doing what you're doing.

00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:50.472
Bender! Here, boy!

00:18:50.473 --> 00:18:52.641
Who wants a Bendy Brew?

00:18:52.642 --> 00:18:54.518
- We'll never find him.

00:18:54.519 --> 00:18:57.021
There must be a
billion robots in here.

00:18:57.022 --> 00:19:00.233
- Then, mathematically, at
least 10 of them must be Bender.

00:19:02.902 --> 00:19:05.821
- Did somebody order something?
- Probably.

00:19:07.616 --> 00:19:10.200
- What happened? Did
you shut down Invasa?

00:19:10.201 --> 00:19:13.329
- Oh, no, no. No off button.
Let's just get outta here.

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:16.332
- Not without Bender! But
we don't know where he is.

00:19:16.333 --> 00:19:18.834
Would you like
directions to Bender?

00:19:18.835 --> 00:19:19.835
PROFESSOR, LEELA, FRY: Yes!

00:19:21.713 --> 00:19:23.714
Make a
slight left, then...

00:19:23.715 --> 00:19:24.965
swerve right suddenly!

00:19:27.010 --> 00:19:29.386
In 100 feet, turn up.

00:19:33.183 --> 00:19:36.727
- Ugh! It always makes you turn
where there's no traffic light.

00:19:36.728 --> 00:19:40.105
In five seconds, you will
collide with your destination.

00:19:40.106 --> 00:19:41.482
- Uh, I don't see him.

00:19:41.483 --> 00:19:43.067
Ow!

00:19:43.068 --> 00:19:45.819
Bender!

00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:48.405
I was so worried about you.

00:19:48.406 --> 00:19:50.908
- Then why'd you run me over?

00:19:52.994 --> 00:19:55.037
- Stop clowning around, Bender.

00:19:55.038 --> 00:19:58.916
Our only hope for escape is to
bust through the outer dome.

00:19:58.917 --> 00:20:01.044
Full speed ahead!

00:20:08.593 --> 00:20:12.513
- Impact in five, four, three...

00:20:12.514 --> 00:20:14.098
four, five?

00:20:14.099 --> 00:20:16.767
- What's happening? Why
are you counting like me?

00:20:16.768 --> 00:20:17.851
- I-I don't know.

00:20:17.852 --> 00:20:20.437
Somehow, we're getting
even further from the dome!

00:20:20.438 --> 00:20:22.940
- Sweet vampire Moses.

00:20:22.941 --> 00:20:26.068
The warehouse is growing
faster than we're traveling.

00:20:26.069 --> 00:20:29.196
- Then there's no possible
way out. We're doomed.

00:20:29.197 --> 00:20:30.531
- Doomed!

00:20:30.532 --> 00:20:31.532
- I go next.

00:20:31.533 --> 00:20:33.409
Doomed!

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:36.120
- Hey, look. There's
Planet Express.

00:20:46.506 --> 00:20:48.674
- Hey! The second moon is gone!

00:20:48.675 --> 00:20:50.551
- Because we're inside of it.

00:20:50.552 --> 00:20:53.387
The Momazon warehouse
now contains

00:20:53.388 --> 00:20:56.473
the entire Earth!

00:20:56.474 --> 00:20:59.768
- Although on the upside, their
deliveries will be even faster now.

00:20:59.769 --> 00:21:03.105
- But on the downside,
it's blotting out the sun.

00:21:03.106 --> 00:21:05.983
We'll freeze to
death within minutes.

00:21:05.984 --> 00:21:07.901
It's always something.

00:21:07.902 --> 00:21:09.695
- I warned you
this would happen!

00:21:09.696 --> 00:21:11.697
- You said global warming!

00:21:11.698 --> 00:21:13.366
- I said climate crisis!

00:21:18.371 --> 00:21:19.913
- I guess this is the end.

00:21:19.914 --> 00:21:23.083
And after all that work
furnishing the apartment.

00:21:23.084 --> 00:21:24.586
- Goodbye, Leela.

00:21:29.799 --> 00:21:32.009
- Ugh, now what?

00:21:35.013 --> 00:21:38.390
The warehouse is
expanding beyond the sun!

00:21:38.391 --> 00:21:40.643
Mars! Jupiter!

00:21:40.644 --> 00:21:43.062
The one with the
onion rings!

00:21:46.608 --> 00:21:47.900
- Good Lord!

00:21:47.901 --> 00:21:51.445
The warehouse smell is
tremendously redshifted!

00:21:51.446 --> 00:21:52.529
- Red-what'd?

00:21:52.530 --> 00:21:54.281
- If these smells are correct,

00:21:54.282 --> 00:21:57.868
it will soon contain the
entire known universe!

00:21:57.869 --> 00:22:01.372
- Oh no! So we're trapped
here in the universe forever?

00:22:01.373 --> 00:22:04.124
- I'm afraid so.
Everything will be

00:22:04.125 --> 00:22:07.170
exactly as bad as
it's always been.

00:22:10.715 --> 00:22:12.883
I understand
you're celebrating.

00:22:12.884 --> 00:22:14.802
Would you like to
purchase champagne?

00:22:14.803 --> 00:22:17.054
- Yes! With someone
else's money.

00:22:20.058 --> 00:22:21.850
- Wait, I'm confused.

00:22:21.851 --> 00:22:24.645
Momazon still works?
But where is it?

00:22:24.646 --> 00:22:26.063
- Everywhere!

00:22:26.064 --> 00:22:28.274
It's my universe now.

00:22:28.275 --> 00:22:30.484
You just shop in it.

00:22:30.485 --> 00:22:32.319
- I mean, it is
convenient though.

00:22:35.323 --> 00:22:36.657
- So much better.

00:22:36.658 --> 00:22:39.451
- Yeah. I returned all
that junky furniture.

00:22:39.452 --> 00:22:41.996
Just kept the empty boxes.

00:22:41.997 --> 00:22:43.664
And the cardboard

00:22:43.665 --> 00:22:45.874
is actually much
sturdier.

00:22:45.875 --> 00:22:48.585
- Hey, roomies. I moved
all my stuff back in.

00:22:48.586 --> 00:22:49.837
- What stuff?

00:22:49.838 --> 00:22:51.922
- Me! I'm my own stuff, baby.

00:22:51.923 --> 00:22:53.716
- Well, we're glad you're back.

00:22:53.717 --> 00:22:57.011
- And we promise to be more
sensitive to your feelings.

00:22:57.012 --> 00:22:58.637
You're not a third wheel.

00:22:58.638 --> 00:23:00.306
- The hell I'm not!

00:23:00.307 --> 00:23:02.600
Working in a tight-knit
collaborative team

00:23:02.601 --> 00:23:05.227
made me realize I hate
being part of a team!

00:23:05.228 --> 00:23:07.104
I prefer being a third wheel.

00:23:07.105 --> 00:23:09.565
- Good. Because you're
totally a third wheel.

00:23:09.566 --> 00:23:11.358
Just pretend
I'm not even here.

00:23:13.862 --> 00:23:15.904
Ahh...